# Homebrew services started at the end of a bootstrap, by setup.sh's `services`
# step. One formula name per line; `#` comments and blank lines are ignored.
#
# Each is started only when brew actually has the formula installed, and that
# guard is the point of this file rather than a detail of it. The two lines it
# replaces were unconditional:
#
#     brew services start atuin
#     brew services start borders
#
# Neither holds on every host:
#
#   atuin    brew formula on mac-mini (homebrew/mac-mini:44) and macbook-2019
#            (:17), but mise-managed on macbook-m5-pro (config/mise/mise.toml:22)
#            and absent from its Brewfile entirely
#   borders  only in macbook-2019's Brewfile (:301, felixkratz/formulae/borders);
#            not installed on macbook-m5-pro or mac-mini
#
# So on macbook-m5-pro both lines failed and on mac-mini one did. They sat
# second-to-last under `set -e`, which means the final `echo "Setup complete."`
# was unreachable on two of three machines — the run always ended one line early
# with a non-zero status and no summary saying why.

atuin
borders
